leafLabelStyleHint:'A style code consists of digits and anchor characters.<br/>Digits: <b>1</b> = restore default, <b>2</b> = italic, <b>3</b> = superscript, <b>4</b> = subscript.<br/>Other characters (including space) = anchor: starting from the current position, find the first matching character in the label text; characters before it get the current style, the anchor itself stays unchanged, and characters after it restore the default style (keeping the original bold/italic setting of the label itself).<br/>Examples (using maize <i>Zea mays</i>; italic parts shown in italics, rest is original):<br/>· Label <code>Zea mays</code>, code <b>2 2</b> or <b>2</b> → <i>Zea mays</i> (both genus and specific epithet italic, taxonomically standard name)<br/>· Label <code>Zea mays</code>, code <b>2 1</b> → <i>Zea</i> mays (only genus italic, specific epithet original)<br/>· Label <code>Zea mays subsp. mays</code>, code <b>2 2 1 2</b> → <i>Zea</i> <i>mays</i> subsp. <i>mays</i> (genus, specific epithet and subspecific epithet italic, subsp. original, taxonomically standard)<br/>· Label <code>Zea mays subsp. mays</code>, code <b>2 2 1</b> → <i>Zea</i> <i>mays</i> subsp. mays (only genus and specific epithet italic)<br/>The <b>Label styles</b> column in the example data table is the style-code example column; you can refer to it directly.<br/>An empty code clears the style of that leaf; re-apply styles after changing the label column.',

